2. Show a Single Create Transaction Modal Prepopulated with All Selected Batches
How it works:
User selects multiple batches in the modal.
When ready, the app opens a single CreateTransactionDialog, prepopulated with all selected batches (e.g., as a table or list inside the dialog).
The user can review/adjust all selections in one place and submit all at once.
Pros:
More efficient for users handling multiple batches at once.
Fewer modal popups, less repetitive clicking.
Can show a summary of all selected batches and allow bulk editing.
Cons:
The dialog UI is more complex (needs to handle a list/table of batches, partial removals, etc.).
Rendering may be slightly slower if there are many batches, but for most use cases (dozens, not thousands), the difference is negligible.
More complex to implement, but better UX for batch operations.
Performance
Single modal for all batches: Slightly more initial rendering if many batches, but React and modern browsers handle tables/lists of dozens or even hundreds of items very efficiently. Unless you expect users to select hundreds/thousands of batches at once, the performance difference is negligible.
